.TH AS 1 "January 15, 1973" "UNIX Fourth Edition" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
v4-as \- assembler
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B as
.RB [ \- ]
.I name ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I as
assembles the concatenation of the named files.
If the optional first argument \fB\-\fR is used, all undefined symbols in the
assembly are treated as global.
.PP
The output of the assembly is written to the file \fBa.out\fR.
It is executable if no errors occurred during the assembly and if there were
no unresolved external references.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/as2
pass 2 of the assembler
.TP
.B /tmp/atm[1-4]?
temporary files
.TP
.B a.out
object file
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBv4-ld\fR(1), \fBv4-aout\fR(5),
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
When an input file cannot be read, its name followed by a question mark is
printed and assembly ceases.
When syntactic or semantic errors occur, a single-character diagnostic is
printed together with the line number and the file name in which it occurred.
Errors in pass 1 cancel pass 2.
The possible errors are:
.TP
.B ")"
Parentheses error
.TP
.B "]"
Parentheses error
.TP
.B "<"
String not terminated properly
.TP
.B "*"
Indirection used illegally
.TP
.B "."
Illegal assignment to \fB.\fR
.TP
.B A
Error in address
.TP
.B B
Branch instruction is odd or too remote
.TP
.B E
Error in expression
.TP
.B F
Error in local (\fBf\fR or \fBb\fR) type symbol
.TP
.B G
Garbage (unknown) character
.TP
.B I
End of file inside an \fBif\fR
.TP
.B M
Multiply defined symbol as label
.TP
.B O
Word quantity assembled at odd address
.TP
.B P
\fB.\fR different in pass 1 and 2
.TP
.B R
Relocation error
.TP
.B U
Undefined symbol
.TP
.B X
Syntax error
.SH BUGS
Symbol table overflow is not checked.
Errors of type \fBX\fR can cause incorrect line numbers in following diagnostics.
